WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.065
Resource Graph holds a copy of
every resource's properties,

2
00:00:04.065 --> 00:00:07.425
in tables you query with
the Kusto Query Language.

3
00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:08.812
It has four traps.

4
00:00:08.812 --> 00:00:11.825
One: an empty result can mean no access.

5
00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:14.394
Microsoft Learn says no results come back

6
00:00:14.394 --> 00:00:16.963
for objects you can't
read, without an error.

7
00:00:16.963 --> 00:00:20.644
So every check reports machines
in scope and empty scope,

8
00:00:20.644 --> 00:00:23.230
the client refuses a query with no scope,

9
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:27.774
and the command line stops when the
identity can see no subscriptions.

10
00:00:27.774 --> 00:00:30.487
Two: paging is a token in the body.

11
00:00:30.487 --> 00:00:32.974
A page holds at most a thousand records;

12
00:00:32.974 --> 00:00:37.013
repeat the same query with the
skip token until none comes back.

13
00:00:37.013 --> 00:00:42.064
Three: some queries can't be paged at
all, when they use limit, sample or take,

14
00:00:42.064 --> 00:00:46.525
or when every output column is
dynamic, as project properties is.

15
00:00:46.525 --> 00:00:50.863
Then the client raises an incomplete
result rather than return part of one.

16
00:00:50.863 --> 00:00:56.462
Four: sort by a unique column, or pages
can repeat some records and skip others.

17
00:00:56.462 --> 00:00:58.937
Every query ends ordered by I D.

18
00:00:58.937 --> 00:01:01.349
And the data isn't strongly consistent,

19
00:01:01.349 --> 00:01:04.490
so a check run minutes after
a change may not see it.
